      "math_academy_id": "e-14378",
      "problem": "Calculate the fourth term of the sequence\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = f(n) -6, \\quad f(1) = 1, \\quad n\\geq 1.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting with the first term $f(1)=1,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the fourth term $f(4).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =1 \\\\ f(2) & =f(1)-6=1-6=-5 \\\\ f(3) & =f(2)-6=-5-6=-11 \\\\ f(4) & =f(3)-6=-11-6=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is $f(4)=-17.$",
